MD simulation of a spring-mass chain surrounded by fluid particles, with periodic boundaries or confining box.

## Program usage
```bash
./md.x paramfile (optional: CUTOFF radius) (optional: apply potential correction (1)) > outfile

time ./md.x param > out1.5.dat && time ./md.x param > out2.0.dat && time ./md.x param > out3.0.dat
time ./md.x param 1.5 0 > 1.5.dat && time ./md.x param 1.5 1 > shift1.5.dat && time ./md.x param 2.0 0 > 2.0.dat && time ./md.x param 2.0 1 > shift2.0.dat && time ./md.x param 3.0 0 > 3.0.dat && time ./md.x param 3.0 1 > shift3.0.dat
```

CUTOFF radii can be deduced by choosing the desired potential energy cutoff.
$$ U(R) = \frac{c}{R^{10}}$$
$$U(R') = \alpha U(R_0) \text{     with an appropriate fraction  } \alpha \sim 1/100$$
$$\frac{c}{R'^{10}} = \alpha \frac{c}{R_0^{10}}$$
which gives a parameter scale that depends on the original chain lenght:
$$ R' = \left( 1/\alpha\right)^{10} R_0 $$
The distance between atoms in the chain is of order $R\sim 2 \AA$ which yields $R_{cutoff} \sim 3.17 \AA$


## Plotting
```gnuplot
gnuplot > p 'out1.5.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'no cut', '1.5.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'cutoff', 'shift1.5.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'cutoff + shift'
gnuplot > p 'out2.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'no cut', '2.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'cutoff', 'shift2.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'cutoff + shift'
gnuplot > p 'out3.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'no cut', '3.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'cutoff', 'shift3.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'cutoff + shift'


gnuplot > p '1.5.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'cut=1.5A' ,'2.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'cut=2.0A', '3.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'cut=3.0A'

gnuplot > p 'out1.5.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'no shift', 'newout1.5.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t 'U(cutoff) = 0'

gnuplot > p 'out1.5.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t '1.5A (no shift)', 'newout1.5.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t '1.5A (shifted)', 'out2.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t '2.0A (no shift)', 'newout2.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t '2.0A (shifted)', 'out3.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t '3.0A (no shift)', 'newout3.0.dat' u 1:4 w l lw 2 t '3.0A (shifted)'
```
